WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.290
A paragraph scrolls past.

2
00:00:02.340 --> 00:00:06.860
One sentence, adding clause
after clause after clause,

3
00:00:06.910 --> 00:00:09.150
and still it keeps going.

4
00:00:09.200 --> 00:00:12.640
Then a single word drops
onto a line of its own.

5
00:00:12.690 --> 00:00:14.870
Forty words slid past.

6
00:00:14.920 --> 00:00:17.030
One word stopped you dead.

7
00:00:17.080 --> 00:00:21.010
So why does a sentence
that short land so hard?

8
00:00:21.060 --> 00:00:24.010
In this mission, you'll
meet four sentence forms:

9
00:00:24.060 --> 00:00:27.800
simple, compound, complex and minor.

10
00:00:27.850 --> 00:00:30.510
You'll watch how Dickens
builds his sentences,

11
00:00:30.560 --> 00:00:34.870
as a stranger rises from among
the graves in Great Expectations.

12
00:00:34.920 --> 00:00:38.350
And you'll rank three
answers about a winter swim.

13
00:00:38.400 --> 00:00:41.260
Is it just the pause a full stop forces?

14
00:00:41.310 --> 00:00:45.900
Your mission: explain why one
short sentence lands so hard.
